{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Gravity: why things fall","theme":{"background":"#f4f7fb","foreground":"#1d2b3a","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Gravity"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"A pulling force between the Earth and any object. It pulls the object down towards the Earth."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"apple"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"When you let go of an apple, what pulls it down?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Gravity","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Wind","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Sound","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which pulls harder on a falling stone: the Earth or the stone?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The Earth pulls harder on the stone","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"The stone pulls harder on the Earth","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Both pull equally","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"ship"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"Mia drops a ball from a tall ship. Should she check the ball's speed or watch where it lands?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Check its speed","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Watch where it lands","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Mia times the ball. It speeds up as it falls, because gravity keeps pulling it down."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Mia sees the ball land on the deck. Gravity pulled it straight down to the Earth."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Weight"},{"type":"text","id":"c7-e","content":"How strongly gravity pulls on an object. Heavier objects have more weight."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"moon"},{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"What keeps the Moon moving around the Earth?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Gravity between the Earth and the Moon","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Magnets in the Moon","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Wind in space","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"If you drop a book and a feather on the Earth at the same time, what happens?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Gravity pulls both down, but air slows the feather","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"The feather floats up","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Only the book falls","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which way does gravity pull an object on Earth?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Towards the centre of the Earth","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Up into the sky","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Sideways across the ground","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the gravity lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Gravity pulls every object towards the Earth. Keep asking why things fall."}],"actions":[]}}
